' =====================================================================
' FLEET STRATEGIES -- the user asked specifically about these.
' Verified: they don't touch CommunityMachine / FleetCapability.
' They consume PlannedTask, which is produced by to_planned_task().
' =====================================================================
package "serverV2/fleets/{community,modal,vast}/  (UNTOUCHED)" <<Frame>> #E0E7FF {

  interface IFleetStrategy <<existing>> {
    + dispatch(task : PlannedTask, ctx, job_id) : DispatchResult
    + cancel(provider_job_id) : None
    + stop_monitoring(job_id) : None
  }

  class CommunityFleetStrategy <<existing>>
  class VastFleetStrategy <<existing>>
  class ModalFleetStrategy <<existing>>

  note bottom of IFleetStrategy #DCFCE7
    **Why these stay untouched**
    Strategies operate on PlannedTask, not on
    CommunityMachine / FleetCapability.
    The Protocol's to_planned_task(...) is the
    seam: planner reads the Protocol, calls
    to_planned_task, hands PlannedTask to the
    strategy.  Strategies never see the source
    target type, so the Protocol refactor is
    invisible to them.
  end note
}

CommunityFleetStrategy ..|> IFleetStrategy
VastFleetStrategy      ..|> IFleetStrategy
ModalFleetStrategy     ..|> IFleetStrategy

' =====================================================================
' DOWNSTREAM OF THE PLANNER -- dispatch_queue + dispatch + orchestrator
' Stores PlannedTask rows, dispatched via fleet strategies.  Also UNTOUCHED.
' =====================================================================
package "serverV2/allocation_dispatch + orchestrator  (UNTOUCHED)" <<Frame>> #E0E7FF {

  class DispatchQueueRepository <<existing>> {
    + enqueue(task : PlannedTask, ctx) : None
    + dequeue_for_fleet(fleet) : DispatchQueueRow_or_None
    .. row carries serialized PlannedTask fields ..
  }
  class AllocationDispatcher <<existing>> {
    + dispatch_one(task : PlannedTask, ctx, job_id) : DispatchResult
    .. picks strategy via task.fleet ; no target type knowledge ..
  }
  class AllocationDispatchQueueService <<existing>> {
    + enqueue(group_id, tasks, ctx) : list of DispatchResult
    + dispatch_pending_for_fleet(fleet) : None
    .. operates on dispatch_queue rows + PlannedTask ..
  }
  class RenderLifecycle <<existing>> {
    + orchestrator entry; never sees AllocationTarget
  }
}

AllocationDispatcher --> IFleetStrategy : routes by task.fleet
AllocationDispatchQueueService --> AllocationDispatcher
AllocationDispatchQueueService --> DispatchQueueRepository : dequeue
RenderLifecycle --> AllocationPlanner : plans here, dispatches downstream

' Upstream + downstream flow around the planner
PendingAllocationRepository  --> AllocationPendingTickProcessor : claim_next
AllocationPendingTickProcessor --> AllocationPlanner : plan_initial / plan_retry
AllocationPlanner            --> DispatchQueueRepository : enqueue(PlannedTask)
FleetAvailabilitySnapshot    --> AllocationPlanner : targets fed in via AvailableResources

