MachinesRouter --> FleetAvailabilitySnapshot : reads

' =====================================================================
note as ScopeNote #FEF9C3
  **Blast radius**
  Modified by the Protocol refactor:
    - serverV2/core/models.py (Protocol + computed @property accessors on both classes)
    - allocation_planner.py (9 isinstance branches removed)
    - allocation_engine_compatibility_validator.py
        (2 isinstance branches removed)
  Untouched:
    - pending_allocation_queue + PendingAllocationRepository
        + AllocationPendingTickProcessor (upstream of the planner;
        rows carry frame range / engine / tier / exclusions, no targets)
    - dispatch_queue + DispatchQueueRepository
        (downstream of the planner; rows are serialized PlannedTask)
    - All 3 fleet strategies (operate on PlannedTask, never on the targets)
    - AllocationDispatcher + AllocationDispatchQueueService (dispatch is PlannedTask-only)
    - Orchestrator / RenderLifecycle (calls planner; never inspects targets)
    - Fleet-availability builders / snapshots / cache / mutable snapshot
        (construct + transport + serdes the concrete types as-is)
    - MachineRepository (still returns CommunityMachine)
    - MachinesRouter (reads concrete fields from the snapshot)
    - Callback / HTTP boundary (operates on jobs, never on targets)
end note

note as SeamNote #DBEAFE
  **The seam that contains the refactor**
  The Protocol's only output to non-planner code is
  the PlannedTask produced by to_planned_task(...).
  Every dispatch / orchestration / callback path
  downstream consumes PlannedTask, which is unchanged
  by the refactor.  The Protocol is a planner-internal
  abstraction with a typed dataclass exit point.
end note

@enduml
